{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21526472",
      "title": "How To (Not) Send Http Requests",
      "lectureOrder": 155,
      "videoOrder": 135,
      "sourceHash": "f9c0f0744c40e9e5a821b8a3a58efb0ab66475946fdecaf11f1ceae11e4fec5b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 3.5,
          "en": "So with Firebase set up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.5,
          "end": 6.88,
          "en": "how do we communicate with it or with any backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.88,
          "end": 8.403,
          "en": "from inside our Vue App?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.41,
          "end": 11.44,
          "en": "We actually, accidentally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.44,
          "end": 16.05,
          "en": "already saw a way of sending HTTP requests earlier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.05,
          "end": 20.01,
          "en": "In our form, the learning survey component here in the form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.01,
          "end": 21.99,
          "en": "there we have a submit button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.99,
          "end": 24.99,
          "en": "And I mentioned earlier in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.99,
          "end": 27.54,
          "en": "that we wanna prevent the browser default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.54,
          "end": 29.38,
          "en": "when that form is being submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.38,
          "end": 33.283,
          "en": "because if we don't do this, a HTTP request would be sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.26,
          "end": 38.17,
          "en": "If I remove the prevent modifier here, temporarily,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.17,
          "end": 43.17,
          "en": "reload and click Submit, watch this reload icon here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.35,
          "end": 47.06,
          "en": "You see it briefly turned into a cross.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.06,
          "end": 48.6,
          "en": "Every time I click this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.6,
          "end": 52.86,
          "en": "what happens is that the browser uses its default behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.86,
          "end": 55.623,
          "en": "which is, to send a HTTP request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.84,
          "end": 58.2,
          "en": "The problem just is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.2,
          "end": 61.24,
          "en": "it's not sending that request to our backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.24,
          "end": 63.3,
          "en": "to our Firebase servers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.3,
          "end": 66.403,
          "en": "but instead it sends the request to the same address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.403,
          "end": 68.82300000000001,
          "en": "that was used for serving this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.66,
          "end": 74.52,
          "en": "And with Vue applications that is typically not the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.52,
          "end": 76.39,
          "en": "that should handle this request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.39,
          "end": 80.42,
          "en": "In this case it's our local computer and our local computer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.42,
          "end": 84.2,
          "en": "does not have any code expecting this request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.2,
          "end": 87.193,
          "en": "So therefore this default request goes into the white.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.03999999999999,
          "end": 91.25,
          "en": "Now you could be building applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.25,
          "end": 93.5,
          "en": "where you also use Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.5,
          "end": 97.13,
          "en": "where your Vue App is served by the same server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.13,
          "end": 99.00999999999999,
          "en": "that should be handling the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.00999999999999,
          "end": 101.773,
          "en": "In that case this browser default might be fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.89,
          "end": 105.21000000000001,
          "en": "But in the vast majority of cases,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.21000000000001,
          "end": 108.63,
          "en": "you'll have a separate server for your Vue App,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.63,
          "end": 112.61,
          "en": "which is just delivering this Vue App to your users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.61,
          "end": 115.97999999999999,
          "en": "then you have free handling of the user data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.97999999999999,
          "end": 118.22,
          "en": "And that's exactly the scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.22,
          "end": 121.25,
          "en": "where you don't want this browser default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.25,
          "end": 123.31,
          "en": "but where instead you wanna prevent it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.31,
          "end": 127.13,
          "en": "and handle the submitted data in JavaScript with Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.13,
          "end": 129.488,
          "en": "For example, also to validate it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.488,
          "end": 132.56,
          "en": "and show such a client site error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.56,
          "end": 135.62,
          "en": "So show this error paragraph, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.62,
          "end": 137.59,
          "en": "that is something you might wanna do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.59,
          "end": 140.89,
          "en": "And once you validate it you then wanna take the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.89,
          "end": 143.75,
          "en": "and send it to the server of your choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.75,
          "end": 146.3,
          "en": "not necessarily to the same server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.3,
          "end": 148.053,
          "en": "that is serving this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.99,
          "end": 151.123,
          "en": "And that's exactly what we wanna do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.96,
          "end": 155.27,
          "en": "So how do we send a request to Firebase then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.27,
          "end": 158.61,
          "en": "which is our chosen backend in this case?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.61,
          "end": 161.38,
          "en": "Well, the nice thing about this Firebase servers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.38,
          "end": 163.32,
          "en": "and they're the real time database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.32,
          "end": 167.16,
          "en": "is that it has this HTTP address which you see here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.16,
          "end": 170.87,
          "en": "And if you send the request of a specific format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.87,
          "end": 175.05,
          "en": "to this address, the data will automatically be picked up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.05,
          "end": 178.09300000000002,
          "en": "by Firebase and will be written to a database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.31,
          "end": 183,
          "en": "Now, it might look like we're directly talking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183,
          "end": 186.27,
          "en": "to a database with that, but we actually aren't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.27,
          "end": 190.28,
          "en": "This is a HTTP address that leads to some server side code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.28,
          "end": 193.72,
          "en": "which we can't see, which was written by the Firebase team,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.72,
          "end": 197.64,
          "en": "which passes the request that will be sent by us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.64,
          "end": 202.09,
          "en": "and then extracts data and then writes it to a database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 202.09,
          "end": 205.11,
          "en": "So for us, it will look like we're directly talking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 205.11,
          "end": 208.13,
          "en": "to a database, but we actually aren't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 208.13,
          "end": 211.63,
          "en": "But this is the address or part of the address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 211.63,
          "end": 214.09,
          "en": "to which we wanna send the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 214.09,
          "end": 215.95,
          "en": "And of course make sure you pick the address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.95,
          "end": 218.98,
          "en": "you are seeing in your dashboard. Not mine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 218.98,
          "end": 221.82,
          "en": "This address will not be available anymore when you're",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 221.82,
          "end": 222.883,
          "en": "viewing this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 224.43,
          "end": 226.63,
          "en": "So we wanna send a request to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 226.63,
          "end": 228.93,
          "en": "But how do we now send the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 228.93,
          "end": 231.28300000000002,
          "en": "from inside our Vue code here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 232.73,
          "end": 235.39,
          "en": "Well, there are a couple of options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 235.39,
          "end": 239.34,
          "en": "We can use third party packages like axios,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 239.34,
          "end": 243.28,
          "en": "which is a very popular JavaScript package for sending",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 243.28,
          "end": 246.9,
          "en": "HTTP requests from inside JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 246.9,
          "end": 249.91,
          "en": "It's very powerful and very easy to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 249.91,
          "end": 251.523,
          "en": "and definitely worth a look.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 252.684,
          "end": 256.13,
          "en": "Alternatively, browsers also have built-in methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256.13,
          "end": 258.28,
          "en": "for sending HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 258.28,
          "end": 261.61,
          "en": "Precisely there is the fetch method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 261.61,
          "end": 264.64,
          "en": "which sounds like it's only there to fetch data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 264.64,
          "end": 267.61,
          "en": "but it's actually a function that allows us to send data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 267.61,
          "end": 269.023,
          "en": "to servers as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 270.28,
          "end": 273.87,
          "en": "Fetch takes a URL as a first argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 273.87,
          "end": 277.47,
          "en": "and then we can configure it to get data from that URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 277.47,
          "end": 279.703,
          "en": "or to send data to that URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 280.54,
          "end": 283.38,
          "en": "And I'm going to work with Fetch here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 283.38,
          "end": 285.02,
          "en": "since it's built into the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 285.02,
          "end": 289.063,
          "en": "but you could absolutely also look into packages like axios.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 290.05,
          "end": 293.31,
          "en": "Both axios and fetch will send so-called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 293.31,
          "end": 296.25,
          "en": "behind the scenes HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 296.25,
          "end": 299.49,
          "en": "That means that we won't reload the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 299.49,
          "end": 303.3,
          "en": "our application will not be killed and restarted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 303.3,
          "end": 306.411,
          "en": "instead the Vue application will continue running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 306.411,
          "end": 311.12,
          "en": "and the HTTP request is just sent well behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 311.12,
          "end": 312.99,
          "en": "to our backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 312.99,
          "end": 315.7,
          "en": "And that's exactly the behavior we want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 315.7,
          "end": 319.6,
          "en": "We want to ensure that our request is sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 319.6,
          "end": 321.963,
          "en": "without restarting the application.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
